This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   - **Standing original request (from prior context)**: "那先重建镜像，然后继续推进" — rebuild the Docker image first, then continue pushing forward with the protobuf migration plan (Stage 4a/4b/4c).
   - **Standing constraint I flagged and have NOT been released from**: Stage 4c (deleting `.msg` files and rosidl publish code) is blocked until the user explicitly confirms no third-party system still subscribes to the old rosidl topic names. `ros2 topic info -v` only shows the local DDS graph and cannot reveal external subscription intent.
   - **In this segment, user sent "继续" / "继续啊" / "完整做完"** — clearly signalling: stop pausing between steps, finish the Stage 4b work completely in one pass.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Stage 4b = making "publish only proto / only rosidl / both" a **parameter**, by absorbing the nodes' self-created rosidl publishers into the dual publisher. This is a **code-level operation**, not a parameter-level one — the nodes previously held two independent handles, so deleting the rosidl publish line could not be done by any runtime switch.
   - `ProtoDualPublisher<RosidlMsgT, ProtoT>` (normal node) and `ProtoLifecycleDualPublisher<RosidlMsgT, ProtoT>` (lifecycle node) each gained `bool rosidl_enabled = true` ctor param, `rosidl_enabled()`, `rosidl_topic()`, and `PublishAll(const RosidlMsgT &)`.
   - New node parameter name: **`proto_rosidl_publish`** (default `true`), independent of `proto_dual_publish`.
   - DDS silently gives no error when a rosidl topic loses all publishers — subscribers just wait forever. Hence the `RCLCPP_WARN` emitted when rosidl side is disabled.
   - Two-level build concurrency limiting: `colcon --parallel-workers` only limits package-level; `CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL` limits per-package make/ninja.
   - `scripts/gcc_mem_guard.sh` — single-process (per-TU) fallback injected via `CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER`, adds `--param ggc-min-expand=10 --param ggc-min-heapsize=32768` to shrink GCC's internal GC heap. **Default OFF** (`AMR_GCC_MEM_GUARD=1` to enable).
   - ccache must be outermost in the launcher chain so GC params don't enter the cache key.
   - Docker container cgroup v2 `memory.max` is the real limit inside a container; `/proc/meminfo` reports the host.
   - `docker restart` preserves the writable layer; `docker compose up -d` recreates it — the reason a manually-`apt-get`-installed `libprotobuf.so.32` seemed "fixed" then vanished.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`src/amr_dispatcher_ros/include/amr_dispatcher_ros/proto_dual_publisher.hpp`** (modified, UNCOMMITTED)
     - The core Stage 4b enabler. Constructor gained `bool rosidl_enabled = true`; rosidl publisher is now owned here:
       ```cpp
       ProtoDualPublisher(
         rclcpp::Node * node, const std::string & rosidl_name, std::size_t qos_depth, bool enabled,
         bool rosidl_enabled = true)
       : rosidl_topic_(rosidl_name),
         proto_topic_(ProtoTopicName(rosidl_name)),
         enabled_(enabled),
         rosidl_enabled_(rosidl_enabled)
       {
         if (rosidl_enabled_) {
           rosidl_pub_ = node->create_publisher<RosidlMsgT>(rosidl_topic_, rclcpp::QoS(qos_depth));
         }
         if (!enabled_) {
           return;
         }
         pub_ = node->create_publisher<ProtoT>(proto_topic_, rclcpp::QoS(qos_depth));
       }
       ```
     - Added `rosidl_enabled()`, `rosidl_topic()`, and:
       ```cpp
       bool PublishAll(const RosidlMsgT & msg)
       {
         bool published = false;
         if (rosidl_pub_) {
           rosidl_pub_->publish(msg);
           published = true;
         }
         if (Publish(msg)) {
           published = true;
         }
         return published;
       }
       ```
     - Members: `bool rosidl_enabled_{true}; typename rclcpp::Publisher<RosidlMsgT>::SharedPtr rosidl_pub_;`

   - **`src/amr_dispatcher_ros/include/amr_dispatcher_ros/proto_lifecycle_dual_publisher.hpp`** (modified, UNCOMMITTED)
     - Same ctor param + `PublishAll`. Critically, `Activate()`/`Deactivate()` now forward to BOTH publishers, because if only proto were activated the node would show "rosidl silent, proto publishing" — the exact mirror-image bug the file's header comment warns about:
       ```cpp
       void Activate()
       {
         if (rosidl_pub_) { rosidl_pub_->on_activate(); }
         if (pub_) { pub_->on_activate(); }
       }
       ```
     - Members: `bool rosidl_enabled_{true}; typename rclcpp_lifecycle::LifecyclePublisher<RosidlMsgT>::SharedPtr rosidl_pub_;`

   - **`src/amr_dispatcher_ros/src/link_health_publisher.cpp`** (MODIFIED, COMPLETE — simplest migration, done as the pattern prototype)
     - Added `declare_parameter("proto_rosidl_publish", true);` with comment "阶段 4b：rosidl 侧开关（默认开）。设为 false 后本节点只发布 *_proto，DDS 里不再出现 /system/aggregated_link_health——这就是「切流」。"
     - Added `const bool proto_rosidl_publish = get_parameter("proto_rosidl_publish").as_bool();`
     - Replaced the separate `aggregated_pub_ = create_publisher<...>` block + dual publisher with:
       ```cpp
       aggregated_proto_pub_ = std::make_unique<ProtoDualPublisher<
           amr_dispatcher_interfaces::msg::ChassisLinkHealth,
           amr_dispatcher::proto::ChassisLinkHealth>>(
           this, "/system/aggregated_link_health", 10, proto_dual_publish,
           proto_rosidl_publish);
       if (aggregated_proto_pub_->enabled()) { RCLCPP_INFO(...); }
